//! Spacing combining marks that share their base character's cell.
//!
//! `unicode-width` gives a spacing mark (general category Mc, such as the
//! Bengali vowel sign in "লো") its own column. Claude Code measures text with
//! Bun's `stringWidth`, which keeps it in the grapheme cluster of the base,
//! so it positions the cursor one column left of us per mark and its
//! incremental repaints land on the wrong cells.
//!
//! The table holds every assigned codepoint that Bun 1.3 measures as zero
//! columns after a base character while `unicode-width` measures one: 368
//! Mc marks plus Thai/Lao SARA AM (Lo) and the Tifinagh consonant joiner (Mn).
//! Unassigned codepoints are left to `unicode-width`.

/// Inclusive codepoint ranges, sorted and disjoint.
